446 - Lo, What a Glorious Sight Appears
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 446
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[D7]Lo, [G]what a glorious sight appears To [D7]our believing [G]eyes!
[D7]The [G]earth and seas are passed away, And [D7]the old rolling [G]skies.
And [D7]the old rolling skies, And [G]the old roll[A7]ing [D]skies;
[D7]The [G]earth and seas are passed away, And [Am]the old [D7]rolling [G]skies.
[G]O that will be joyful, [D7]joyful, [G]joyful!
[G]O that will be joyful When we [D7]meet to part no [G]more!
When we [D]meet to part no more on [G]Canaan's hap[A7]py [D]shore;
[D7]'Tis [G]there we'll meet at Jesus' feet, When we [Am]meet to [D7]part no [G]more!

Refrain:
[D7]O [G]that will [D7]be joyful, [G]joyful, joyful!
[D7]O [G]that [D7]will [G]be joyful
[D7]When [G]we meet [A7]to part [D]no more!
[D7]When [G]we [Am]meet to [D7]part [G]no more
[G]On [D7]Canaan's [G]happy shore;
[G]'Tis there [D7]we'll meet [G]at Jesus' feet,
[D]When [G]we meet [A7]to part [D]no more!

Verse 2:
[D7]Attending [G]angels [D7]shout [G]for joy
[D7]And [G]the [D7]bright [G]armies sing-
[D7]Mortals! [G]Behold [A7]the [D]sacred seat
[D7][G]Of [Am]your [D7]descending [G]King.
[G]Of [D7]your [G]descending King,
[G]Of [D7]your [G]descending King;
[D]Mortals! [G]Behold [A7]the [D]sacred seat
[D7][G]Of [Am]your [D7]descending [G]King.

Verse 3:
[D7]His own [G]soft hand [D7]shall wipe [G]the tears
[D7]From [G]every [D7]weeping [G]eye;
[D7]And pains, [G]and groans, [A7]and griefs, [D]and fears,
[D7]And [G]death [Am]itself [D7]shall [G]die!
[G]And [D7]death itself [G]shall die,
[G]And [D7]death itself [G]shall die;
[D]And pains, [G]and groans, [A7]and griefs, [D]and fears,
[D7]And [G]death [Am]itself [D7]shall [G]die.

Verse 4:
[D7]How [G]long, dear [D7]Savior! Oh, [G]how long
[D7]Shall [G]this [D7]bright [G]hour delay?
[D7]Fly [G]swifter round, [A7]ye wheels [D]of time!
[D7]And [G]bring [Am]the [D7]welcome [G]day.
[G]And [D7]bring the [G]welcome day,
[G]And [D7]bring the [G]welcome day;
[D]Fly [G]swifter round, [A7]ye wheels [D]of time!
[D7]And [G]bring [Am]the [D7]welcome [G]day.
